[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3601578848","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113342#issuecomment-3601578848","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113342","id":3601578848,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Wq7tg","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-02T11:32:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-02T11:34:20Z","body":"> But, for ease of use, I think `profiler` should be deduced if not explicitly provided, using the previous logic. I really liked that I _didn't_ have to write explicitly which profiler should be used, in addition to the path.\r\n\r\nI don't know, my suggestion to add `profiler` was to avoid doing this kind of magic path recognition.\r\n\r\nI would prefer adding quality of life improvements in the other direction: pass `profiler=tracy`, and have it automatically find the Tracy SDK in `bin/build_deps/tracy` downloaded via `misc/scripts/download_tracy_sdk.py`. `profiler_path` would remain as an advanced option for folks who want to keep their profiler out of tree (e.g. 